Meeting summary for 4 March 2026:

  *

    *Updated: forums situation*
    The new forums are now live. If you had an account there you will
    need to reset your password and reactivate your account.
    At the moment it has a header/footer that are very corporatey (the
    work was done by OpenVPN Inc.) but this will be adjusted to
    community stuff.
    Further improvements and adjustments will be made in the coming days
    and weeks.
    For more information
    see:https://forums.openvpn.net/d/46497-welcome-to-the-new-openvpn-community-forum

  *

    *Updated: OpenVPN 2.7 release*
    We have some minor bugfixes lined up for the next bugfix release
    2.7.1. Intention is to do a 2.7.1 release around 11 March or so.
    There is one issue under investigation when using multisocket, where
    with many clients, responses are slow.
    This is still an ongoing investigation as it's not straight-forward
    to reproduce.

  *

    *Updated: community meetup 2026*
    Coordination is currently taking place
    here:https://community.openvpn.net/Meetups/2026-Paderborn
    The date is around 17 and 18 October, location in Paderborn, Germany.

As always you're welcome to join at #openvpn-meeting on Libera IRC 
network every Wednesday at 14:00 Central European Time.

Kind regards,
Johan Draaisma

